  "result": "`python3 -m shop quote a:12.5:2` now prints 27.06. All 6 tests pass. I ran them with `unittest` because `pytest` isn't installed.\n\n**Root cause:** `to_cents` in `shop/money.py` padded a one-digit fraction on the left. So `\"12.5\"` became `12.05` (1205 cents) instead of `12.50` (1250 cents), and the quote came out as 26.09. I changed `frac.rjust(2, \"0\")` to `frac.ljust(2, \"0\")`.\n\nI didn't add a test for one-decimal amounts like `12.5`. The existing tests didn't catch this bug.",
